# SHJT_PropofolSleep PRO10 – Multimodal BIDS Dataset

## Dataset Overview

This dataset contains multimodal neuroimaging data from propofol-induced sleep in mice (PRO10 cohort), organized according to the Brain Imaging Data Structure (BIDS) standard version 1.9.0.

**Data Modalities:**
- **fMRI**: Resting-state functional MRI data from 10 mice (sub-02 to sub-11)
- **EEG**: Raw EEG recordings from 7 mice (sub-12 to sub-18)

**Important Note:** The EEG and fMRI data are **not in a one-to-one correspondence**. They represent independent recordings from different animals within the same experimental cohort (PRO10). This is clearly indicated in the `participants.tsv` file under the `data_types` column.

## Dataset Structure

```
fMRI_BIDS/
├── dataset_description.json       # BIDS dataset metadata
├── participants.tsv             # Subject metadata (fMRI + EEG)
├── participants.json             # Metadata column descriptions
├── README                       # This file
├── task-rest_bold.json          # Task-specific JSON (inherited)
├── .bidsignore                 # BIDS ignore file
├── sub-02/ to sub-11/         # fMRI subjects (10 subjects)
│   ├── anat/                   # T2-weighted anatomical images
│   │   ├── sub-XX_T2w.nii.gz
│   │   └── sub-XX_T2w.json
│   └── func/                   # Resting-state BOLD fMRI
│       ├── sub-XX_task-rest_bold.nii.gz
│       └── sub-XX_task-rest_bold.json
├── sub-12/ to sub-18/         # EEG subjects (7 subjects)
│   └── eeg/                   # Raw EEG recordings (EDF format)
│       ├── sub-XX_task-rest_eeg.edf
│       └── sub-XX_task-rest_eeg.json
└── code/                       # Python analysis scripts (see below)
```

## Acquisition Parameters

### fMRI Data
| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Scanner | Bruker BioSpec 94/20, 9.4 T |
| Sequence | Gradient-echo EPI |
| TR | 2000 ms |
| TE | (see individual JSON sidecars) |
| Slices | 30 (axial, interleaved ascending) |
| Slice timing | 0.0 – 1.93 s (30 slices, step = 0.0667 s) |
| Voxel size | (see individual NIfTI headers) |
| Phase encoding direction | j- (anterior–posterior) |
| Subjects | n=10 (sub-02 through sub-11) |

### EEG Data
| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Format | EDF (European Data Format) |
| Sampling frequency | 1000 Hz |
| Channels | 1 (EEG) |
| Power line frequency | 50 Hz |
| Recording type | Continuous |
| Subjects | n=7 (sub-12 through sub-18) |
| Total size | ~176 MB |

